   "id": "54df83c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Forward citations — distributions and windowed monotonicity\n",
    "\n",
    "`C_3 <= C_5 <= C_10 <= C_all` must hold for **every** case: the windows are nested, so a wider\n",
    "window cannot count fewer citations. This is the cheapest end-to-end check on the citation\n",
    "build, and it is asserted rather than eyeballed.\n",
    "\n",
    "The distribution is the familiar heavy tail. Plotted on log–log with zero-citation cases stated\n",
    "separately, because they are 27% of the corpus and a log axis cannot show them."
   ]
  },
  {
