   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "bad = con.execute(f\"\"\"SELECT count(*) FROM read_parquet('{CIT}')\n",
    "  WHERE C_3 > C_5 OR C_5 > C_10 OR C_10 > C_all\"\"\").fetchone()[0]\n",
    "print(f'windowed monotonicity violations: {bad:,}')\n",
    "assert bad == 0, 'C_3 <= C_5 <= C_10 <= C_all is violated — the citation build is wrong'\n",
    "\n",
    "st = con.execute(f\"\"\"SELECT\n",
    "  count(*) AS cases,\n",
    "  count(*) FILTER (WHERE C_all = 0) AS never_cited,\n",
    "  round(avg(C_3),3) AS mean_C_3, round(avg(C_5),3) AS mean_C_5,\n",
    "  round(avg(C_10),3) AS mean_C_10, round(avg(C_all),3) AS mean_C_all,\n",
    "  max(C_all) AS max_C_all FROM read_parquet('{CIT}')\"\"\").fetchdf()\n",
    "display(st)\n",
    "print(f\"never cited: {int(st.never_cited[0]):,} ({st.never_cited[0]/st.cases[0]*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "d = con.execute(f\"\"\"SELECT C_all, count(*) AS n FROM read_parquet('{CIT}')\n",
    "  WHERE C_all > 0 GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1\"\"\").fetchdf()\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4.2), layout='constrained')\n",
    "ax[0].loglog(d.C_all, d.n, '.', ms=3, color=BLUE, alpha=.6)\n",
    "style(ax[0], 'citations (C_all)', 'cases', 'Forward-citation distribution (log-log)')\n",
    "for w, c in (('C_3', BLUE), ('C_5', ORANGE), ('C_10', AQUA), ('C_all', VIOLET)):\n",
    "    dd = con.execute(f\"\"\"SELECT {w} AS v, count(*) AS n FROM read_parquet('{CIT}')\n",
    "      WHERE {w} > 0 GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1\"\"\").fetchdf()\n",
    "    ax[1].loglog(dd.v, dd.n.cumsum() / dd.n.sum(), lw=1.8, color=c, label=w)\n",
    "style(ax[1], 'citations', 'cumulative share of cited cases', 'Nested windows')\n",
    "ax[1].legend(frameon=False, fontsize=9)\n",
    "V.save('3')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ffb178ea",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Mean citations by decision year — and the truncation it exposes\n",
    "\n",
    "The rise-then-collapse at the right of `C_all` is **not** a finding about law. A case decided in\n",
    "2019 has had one year to be cited; one decided in 1980 has had forty. The dashed guide marks\n",
    "where each window closes; to its right the series measures elapsed time, not influence.\n",
    "\n",
    "`C_10` is the honest series for anything up to 2010, and the age profile in §5 is what to use\n",
    "past that."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "3ff04e4e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "/project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/validation/val_common.py:96: UserWarning: The figure layout has changed to tight\n",
      "  fig.tight_layout()\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  [fig] case_law_validation_4.jpg + .pdf  (600 dpi)\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1100x506 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "CPU times: user 1.92 s, sys: 107 ms, total: 2.03 s\n",
      "Wall time: 1.45 s\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "['/project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/validation/Figures/case_law_validation_4.jpg',\n",
       " '/project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/validation/Figures/case_law_validation_4.pdf']"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 5,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "g = con.execute(f\"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT m.decision_year AS year, count(*) AS n,\n",
    "       avg(c.C_3) AS C_3, avg(c.C_5) AS C_5, avg(c.C_10) AS C_10, avg(c.C_all) AS C_all\n",
    "FROM read_parquet('{CIT}') c JOIN read_parquet('{META}') m USING (case_id)\n",
    "WHERE m.decision_year >= 1800 GROUP BY 1 HAVING count(*) >= 100 ORDER BY 1\"\"\").fetchdf()\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 4.6), layout='constrained')\n",
    "# An all-time window never 'closes' -- it gets SHORTER the nearer a case sits to the\n",
    "# snapshot, so it is the series most damaged by truncation, not the least. Mapping it to\n",
    "# 0 disabled the guard on exactly the wrong series. It is given the widest fixed window's\n",
    "# horizon (10y) as a conservative stand-in, and the guide is labelled as a stand-in.\n",
    "CLOSE_H = {'_3': 3, '_5': 5, '_10': 10, '_all': 10}\n",
    "for col, c in (('C_3', BLUE), ('C_5', ORANGE), ('C_10', AQUA), ('C_all', VIOLET)):\n",
    "    sfx = '_' + col.split('_', 1)[1]\n",
    "    closed = SNAP - CLOSE_H[sfx]\n",
    "    s = g[g.year <= closed]; f = g[g.year >= closed]\n",
    "    ax.plot(s.year, s[col], lw=2, color=c,\n",
    "            label=col + (' *' if sfx == '_all' else ''))\n",
    "    ax.plot(f.year, f[col], lw=2, color=c, alpha=.28)\n",
    "    ax.axvline(closed, color=c, lw=.8, ls='--', alpha=.5)\n",
    "style(ax, 'decision year', 'mean citations',\n",
    "      'Mean forward citations by decision year — faint = window not elapsed')\n",
    "ax.legend(frameon=False, fontsize=9)\n",
    "V.save('4')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a3831f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Citation age profile — when a case gets cited\n",
    "\n",
    "From `case_citation_trend.parquet`, which keeps the full history rather than four windows. This\n",
    "is the shape the windows are cutting through, and it is the part of the citation process that\n",
    "truncation does *not* destroy: restricting to cases old enough to have the full age range makes\n",
    "the profile comparable across eras.\n",
    "\n",
    "The right panel splits the profile by decision era. A flattening or lengthening profile over\n",
    "time would mean the windows are not comparable across eras even where they have closed — worth\n",
    "knowing before any window-based claim."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "f8cf8346",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "/project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/validation/val_common.py:96: UserWarning: The figure layout has changed to tight\n",
      "  fig.tight_layout()\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  [fig] case_law_validation_5.jpg + .pdf  (600 dpi)\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1320x484 with 2 Axes>"
